  "responsibility": "Turns the checkout registry into the repositories the navigator lists: each identity's chosen checkout, its vault and its state, and the names of the vaults",
  "description": "An identity is listed when any known checkout has a vault in the .archboard/vault layout; its state is ready, no-vault, gone or unchosen. The registry is the only source: no environment variable names a vault (TASK-472.09). A vault whose link leads out of the layout is no vault here, because every call to it is refused: its checkout reads no-vault, and an untracked one is not listed. The vault a page opens in is that of the first ready repository by name, else none. repositoryOfVault is how a show names the repository a pane moved into. A vault that no registry entry holds has no repository name, and its checkout is the directory that holds it.",
